    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d809">

                <pb facs="1275" n="1261" xml:id="pg1261"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War/10–1044</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the British Ambassador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Halifax</hi>)</head>
                <p>The Secretary of State presents his compliments to His Excellency the British
                    Ambassador and has the honor to refer to the Embassy’s note No. 601, Reference:
                    3136/5/44, dated September 30, 1944, concerning the mistreatment of Allied
                    parachutists who fall into German hands.</p>
                <p>There is transmitted herewith for the Embassy’s information a copy of the
                    Department’s telegram of today’s date to the American Legation at Bern<anchor
                        n="51" xml:id="d809-f1"/> which sets forth the protest which the Swiss
                    Government is being requested to deliver to the German Government in this
                    connection.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-24">October 24,
                            1944</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
